Given a binary array nums and an integer goal, return the number of non-empty subarrays with a sum goal.

A subarray is a contiguous part of the array.




Solution

class Solution {
    public int numSubarraysWithSum(int[] nums, int goal) {
     int n= nums.length;
     int count=0;
     for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
        int sum=0;
        for(int j=i;j<n;j++){
            sum+=nums[j];
            if(sum==goal){
                count++;
            }
        }
     }
     return count;   
    }
}
